# Basic Edition Environment Variables
#
# Change settings with `smoking-pi config set KEY VALUE` (`config list` shows
# them by section, `config describe KEY` explains one), not by editing the
# env file: the command checks the value and restarts what reads it.
# This template is also their schema. `## Name` starts a section; a `#:` line
# describes the key right below it: a type (int, float, bool: true/false/1/0,
# enum:a|b, time, date, tz, url, origin: https://host[:port]), bounds (min=N,
# gt=N: above N, max=N, allow=V: V as well), and flags (secret: shown only on
# request; install: generated or fixed at install, which `config set`
# refuses).

## General
# Timezone configuration
#: tz
TZ=UTC

## SmokePing
# Network configuration
#: int min=1 max=65535
SMOKEPING_PORT=80

## mDNS
# The Pi's name on the LAN (docs/mdns.md): the mdns service answers for
# <MDNS_NAME>.local. Empty = smoking-pi (smoking-pi.local); off = no name.
# A second Smoking Pi on the network gets <name>-2.local: give each its own.
# MDNS_INTERFACES: comma-separated interfaces; empty = every LAN interface.
MDNS_NAME=
MDNS_INTERFACES=

## Volume paths
# Volume paths (optional)
# SMOKEPING_DATA_PATH=/path/to/data
# SMOKEPING_CACHE_PATH=/path/to/cache